72 720 Td
(Zorvatic caching rules) Tj T*
(A Zorvatic cache keeps the most recent answer for each query key.) Tj T*
(Entries expire after one hour, and any write to the underlying table) Tj T*
(invalidates every cached entry that was computed from that table.) Tj T*
(Readers that miss the cache recompute the value and store it again,) Tj T*
(so a burst of misses after an invalidation is expected and harmless.) Tj T*
(Summary: Zorvatic caches are invalidated by writes, not by size.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
